library Management System

Start The Program

Run the Main class.

The system will automatically:
- load users from users.csv
- load items from items.csv

Add Users

Example:
Student student = new Student("0001", "John", new ArrayList<>());
Teacher teacher = new Teacher("0002", "Mike", new ArrayList<>());

library.addUser(student);
library.addUser(teacher);

add Items

Example:

Book book = new Book("Java Basics", "12345", "Smith", "Programming");
DVD dvd = new DVD("Batman", "Nolan", 120);

library.addItem(book);
library.addItem(dvd);

Borrow An Item

Example:
library.borrowItem(student, book);

If successful:
- item status becomes BORROWED

Return An Item

Example:
library.returnItem(student, book);

If successful:
- item status becomes IN_STORE

Search By Title

Example:

List<Item> results = library.searchByTitle("Java");

Search By Author

Example:
List<Book> books = library.searchByAuthor("Smith");

Export Data To CSV

Example:

library.exportAll(
    "src/main/resources/items.csv",
    "src/main/resources/users.csv"
);

This saves all users and items.

Load Data From CSV

Example:
library.loadAll(
    "src/main/resources/items.csv",
    "src/main/resources/users.csv"
);

This reloads all saved data.

Possible Item Status
- IN_STORE
- BORROWED
- LOST
